{"question": "Năng lượng kích hoạt của diode laser cụ thể là bao nhiêu joule khi thực hiện kích hoạt chất bơm rửa trong điều trị viêm quanh chóp?", "claim": "Khi sử dụng diode laser để kích hoạt chất bơm rửa trong điều trị nội nha viêm quanh chóp, cần thiết lập năng lượng chính xác là 1.5W ở chế độ liên tục trong 30 giây.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Tài liệu nội bộ quy định thông số năng lượng khi thực hiện kích hoạt chất bơm rửa bằng diode laser để đạt hiệu quả khử khuẩn tối ưu."}], "conversation": {"history": []}, "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Table 2"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Characteristics and results of included studies"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q3", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Authors | Study type/number of patients/level of VSC | Groups | Laser (nm) + photosensitizer | Protocol aPDT | Study observation—time | Results"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q4", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "5. Ciarcia et al. [19] | RCT 39 patients | G1 = 13 G2 = 13 G3 = 13 G1-aPDT G2- tongue scraper G3- aPDT i scraper | 660 nm methylene blue 0,005% | P = 400 mW E = 36 J t = 90 s P = 1039.4 mW/cm2 density E = 93.5 J/cm2 4 irradiated points, distance: 2 cm, for 2 min | 1 session, immediately after the treatment 1 week 14 days 30 days (VSC level) | Directly after the treatment the significant reduction in VSC was observed No data available after 7, 14, and 30 days"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q5", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "The efficacy of irrigation protocols in endodontic treatment relies heavily on their ability to navigate the complex anatomy of the root canal system and effectively disinfect hard-to-reach areas. Sodium hypochlorite (NaOCl) and ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) remain fundamental irrigants due to their proven antimicrobial properties and ability to remove smear layers. However, advancements in irrigation activation methodologies, such as diode laser-activated irrigation (LAI) and sonic systems like EDDY, have further enhanced their clinical utility. It has been demonstrated that diode lasers significantly enhance antibacterial efficacy through thermophotodisruptive effects; however, their impact on postoperative pain reduction (PP) remains inconclusive, as no statistically significant differences were found between the conventional and advanced protocol groups (27). Similarly, LAI "}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q6", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "showed superior pain reduction compared to photobiostimulation and conventional irrigation within the first 24 h, although differences were not statistically significant beyond this period (28)."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Effectiveness of lasers and aPDT in elimination of intraoral halitosis: a systematic review based on clinical trials", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results", "Results of individual studies"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Efficacy of diode Laser compared to conventional irrigation in endodontic treatment of apical periodontitis: a systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion", "Irrigation protocols and methodologies"]}]}
